I recently did a deep dive on what it means to fear the Lord 

What I learned impacted me greatly as a Christian and God put it on my heart to share it in hopes that it might also change others

My curiosity to understand what it means to fear God began after listening to a Live Free podcast episode with John Bevere

John was telling the story of when he met Jim Baker in prison

For those who don’t know, Jim Baker had one of the largest Christian ministries in the 1980s but became embroiled in financial fraud and scandals which landed him in prison

John Bevere told the story about when he visited Jim in prison

He said he Jim when he stopped loving Jesus and surprisingly, Jim said never. He said the problem wasn't that he didnt Love Jesus, but that he didn’t fear the Lord

In that moment I learned 

1) loving Jesus and fearing God were different things 

and 2) that a failure to fear God has major consequences on how we live

My curiosity led me down a path of inquiry to better understand the concept of fearing God

What does it mean to fear God? 

How is that fear developed? 

How does the fear of God show up in how we behave? 

The Bible does not treat fear of God as an optional extra. Fearing God is not someting we choose to do or not do. As Christians, it's something we MUST do



