Fear of the Lord is written 14 times in the book of Proverbs and shows up 27 times in Scripture. 

That's not a mistake. The repetition is a signal of importance

If God writes something 27 times it's because he wants us to read it 27 times. Through repetition hes telling us it's important and that we should take it seriously


Worth highlighting is the difference between unholy fear (aka worldly fear) and holy fear


Worldly fear is an anxiety-driven dread of losing control, or safety. It stems from a desire to control circumstance and stems from self reliance. This unholy fear can produce panic and anxiety and cause us to hide or run away
from responsibility. It separates us from God

Holy fear is a deep reverence, awe, and love for God that draws a person closer to Him and turns them away from evil. Instead of being afraid of God, holy fear causes us to obey so we don't disappoint our almighty and generous
Father

Holy fear produces hatred for sin. Hatred of evil. It also changes our posture toward God. We stop treating him as our friend or magical genie that grants prayers and begin treating him with reverence, awe and humility

A holy fear of God serves as a moral compass that guides our daily choices. It means having a deep respect, holy reverence,and submission to the Father. It doesnt mean being terrified. 


Spurgeon said there is a fear we must never wish to lose and that is the Holy, filial fear of a child towards a Father who is infinitely great and perfect

Not the fear that runs from God. The fear that runs TO God and will not treat Him lightly


Q1-------> What does it mean to fear God?

It doesn't mean hiding from him like a criminal in the dark, cowering from judgement

Fearing God doesn't mean we live everyday waiting to br struck or beaten

Fearing God means we have finally seen Him as he is. 

We see the Father as holy. Not almost holy. Holy.

We see God as Just. Not mostly just or 99.9% just. Completely and fully just.

We see God as almighty. not impressive. not remarkable. Not exceptional. ALMIGHTY

A Being with complete and total power. Supreme, divine. Almighty. Creator of all things, including us

Having supreme authority, the ability to do all things without limit

And when we finally see God for who He really is. When the creation finally acknowledges the creator with clarity, the heart bows in reverence

That bow. That submission and reverence for the almighty is the fear of the Lord. 


The fear of God is reverent awe that produces obedient love

Reverence is a great word. It means a profound respect mixed with love, devotion and awe

Reverent awe that produces obedient love

That is not the same as being scared of a beating

That is not the same fear of a slave who fears the whip

You see, the slave obeys while the master is watching but the moment the room is empty, the call to obedience goes away

The child of God, on the other hand, fears grieving the Father

We obey because we have seen the Fathers holiness and the Father's mercy

We don't want to wound the one who bled for us

1 John 4:18 says "There is no fear in love, but perfect love casts out fear. For fear has to with with punishment, and whoever fears has not been perfected in love"

The gospel removes fear and terror of condemnation for those who are in Christ

The gospel removes all fear except the fear and trembling of worship. The physical or spiritual shaking that happens when we feel deep holy revrence and awe in the presence of God the supreme master and creator

The difference is that we don't fear God as a tyrant. We fear God as a Father, a King, and a Judge who sees everything





Q2-------> How does the fear of God show up in how we behave? 

Simply put, fearing the Lord produces obedience

It shows up in the secret places. The hidden areas of our lives

The person who fears God doesn't need an audience to do what is right

The person who fears God tells the truth when a lie would be easier

The person who fears God keeps their body holy when nobody else would know

We turn from the joke, the click, the conversation, the bitterness because God is in the room

Proverbs 8:13 says "the fear of the Lord is hatred of evil"

Not management of evil. Not renaming of evil. Hatred of evil

When we lose reverence and fear of God, we loosen our standards and become more accepting of sin

The fear of the Lord shows up in how we treat people

The fear of the Lord shrinks fear of all the other things. Fear of man, fear of illness, fear of poverty, fear of uncertainty, fear of judgement, even fear of death

The fear of God makes us both courageous and kind at the same time

Josh Howerton put it super simply: our lives will be controlled by one of two fears:

The fear of man or the fear of God

Man and God cannot share the same throne, therefore a choice must be made

Choose to fear God and you can accept upsetting or disappointing people because you refuse to disappoint the Father

Fear of God offers us courage and boldness because if we fear God and obey his commandments, we have nothing else to fear




Q3-------> How is that fear developed? 

Its not developed by thinking of the punishment we will receive from disobeying God

It develops by staring at God

The fear of God is developped when we open our Bible and let God speak to us in his own voice

Faith comes by listening. Holy fear comes the same way

Read Gods word until his holiness stops being an empty slogan

Read Gods word until his commands stop being light suggestions

Read until the cross shows you both the cost of sin and the kindness of God

The fear of God is developped in worship that is not entertainment

In prayer that is not a grocery list of boxes to check off

In repentance that is not a casual shrug

The more clearly we see God in his almighty glory, the more carefully we walk. The more carefully we act



I'm almost done. Time to wrap up

Loving God is not enough if love never becomes obedience

REPEAT

In John Chapter 14 verse 15, Jesus says "If you love me, you will keep my commandments"

Jesus says this to his disciples at the last supper shortly before his crucifixion

Jesus is saying that true love for him is not just words or feelings, but actively choosing to obey his teachings

To summarize, Ecclesiastes ends the whole search of life with this:

Fear God

Keep His commandments

We cannot obey what we have not learned so we need to open our Bibles

Know his commandments. understand them, then do them

And when we miss the mark, and we will, don't defend the sin. Dont excuse it. Dont accept it. Dont shrug it off or rename it

Repent. Turn away from it. Confess. Forsake it, abandon it, stop it

Come back to the Father who is both holy and merciful

Fear God

Not fear of the whip. Not fear of punishment

Fear that comes from being in the presence of the almightly majesty of a perfect Father

Know is word

Obey his word

When we fall, repent and turn from sin

That my friends is not bondage

That is the beginning of Wisdom

